.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt NVMF-CONNECT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvmf-connect
.Nd connect to NVMe over Fabrics subsystems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm connect
.Op Fl FGg
.Op Fl c Ar cntlid
.Op Fl i Ar queues
.Op Fl k Ar seconds
.Op Fl l Ar seconds
.Op Fl Q Ar entries
.Op Fl q Ar hostnqn
.Op Fl r Ar seconds
.Op Fl t Ar transport
.Ar address : Ns Ar port
.Ar subnqn
.Nm
.Cm discover
.Op Fl q Ar hostnqn
.Op Fl t Ar transport
.Ar address Ns Op : Ns Ar port
.Nm
.Cm disconnect
.Fl a | Ar subnqn
.Nm
.Cm list
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility connects this system, as a host, to a remote NVM subsystem over
TCP and hands the connection to the
.Xr nvmf_host 4D
driver.
The driver then presents each namespace of the subsystem as a disk
through
.Xr blkdev 4D .
.Pp
The system can be connected to one subsystem at a time.
A connection that is lost is not re-established: use
.Cm disconnect
and then
.Cm connect
again.
.Pp
An
.Ar address
is a host name, an IPv4 address or an IPv6 address.
An IPv6 address that is followed by a port must be enclosed in square
brackets.
.Pp
The host identifies itself with a host NQN and a host ID.
They are read from
.Pa /etc/nvme/hostnqn
and
.Pa /etc/nvme/hostid .
A file that does not exist is created the first time it is needed: the
host ID from the system's SMBIOS UUID, or at random if the system has
none, and the host NQN from the host ID.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ar
.It Cm connect
Connect to the subsystem
.Ar subnqn
at
.Ar address
and
.Ar port .
I/O controllers usually listen on port 4420.
.Bl -tag -width Ar
.It Fl c Ar cntlid
The controller to ask for:
.Sy dynamic ,
.Sy static ,
or a controller ID.
The default is
.Sy dynamic .
.It Fl F
Require submission queue flow control.
.It Fl G
Request data digests.
.It Fl g
Request header digests.
.It Fl i Ar queues
The number of I/O queues.
The default is 1.
.It Fl k Ar seconds
The Keep Alive timeout.
The default is 120 seconds.
.It Fl l Ar seconds
How long the driver waits for a lost connection to be re-established
before it gives up on the controller.
The default is 600 seconds.
.It Fl Q Ar entries
The size of each I/O queue.
The default is 128, or the controller's maximum if that is smaller.
.It Fl q Ar hostnqn
Use
.Ar hostnqn
as the host NQN instead of the one in
.Pa /etc/nvme/hostnqn .
.It Fl r Ar seconds
How often the driver asks for a lost connection to be re-established.
The default is 10 seconds.
.It Fl t Ar transport
The transport.
Only
.Sy tcp
is supported.
.El
.It Cm discover
Print the discovery log of the discovery controller at
.Ar address .
The default
.Ar port
is 8009.
The
.Fl q
and
.Fl t
options are as for
.Cm connect .
.It Cm disconnect
Disconnect from the subsystem
.Ar subnqn
and remove its disks.
The command fails if the system is not connected to that subsystem.
With
.Fl a ,
disconnect whatever is connected.
.It Cm list
Print the connected controller, its address and its namespaces.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
There is no authentication and no TLS.
.Nm
cannot verify that the system it reaches is the intended target, it
cannot connect to a target that requires authentication, and data
crosses the network unencrypted.
Use it only on networks where every system that can reach or
impersonate the target is trusted.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /etc/nvme/hostid
The host ID, as a UUID.
.It Pa /etc/nvme/hostnqn
The host NQN.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Sy Example 1
Finding and connecting to a subsystem
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# nvmf-connect discover 192.168.10.5
# nvmf-connect connect -i 4 192.168.10.5:4420 \e
    nqn.2026-01.com.example:storage:vol0
# nvmf-connect list
.Ed
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
The command line interface of
.Nm
is
.Sy Uncommitted .
The output of
.Nm
is
.Sy Not-An-Interface
and may change at any time.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr blkdev 4D ,
.Xr nvmf_host 4D ,
.Xr nvmfd 8
